          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बाज़ार (bāzār) — \"a market\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian bāzār, a market. English borrowed the same word — bazaar — from the same Persian source, by way of Italian traders."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So this is not a cousin but a shared borrowing: Hindi and English both took it from Persian, separately. You met that shape with चाय, which the world took from Chinese by two different roads."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The third of five, and a word English took from the same place."
            }
          ]
        },
